{
	"$comment": "Required artifacts per platform, verified after packaging and before signing by build/verify/verify-package.mjs. Every path was taken from a walked real package (mac 1.4.9-0084) or from the packaging script line that stages it (win32 beast/helper) — never from memory. shared=true means the artifact must exist on EVERY platform (feature parity); the --parity mode enforces that every shared id is declared everywhere. minBytes is ~half the observed real size, to catch truncated or zero-byte copies. NOTE .v3code is a MIX: skills/, rules/, and mcp/ are shipped product content the runtime resolves at appRoot, everything else in it is dev state — so the required and forbidden lists both point INTO that directory. 'forbidden' paths must NOT exist in a shippable tree (a trailing * is a prefix match on the parent directory's entries; a <dir>/**/*<suffix> pattern matches any file under <dir>, recursively, whose name ends with <suffix>). 'asar' entries assert what lives INSIDE an archive — the one place a file-level tree walk is blind; expect:'empty' pins the current build's behaviour (all modules unpacked) so a future switch to packing them fails loudly instead of passing a tree check while the app cannot resolve them.",
